<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose six points to 1,481.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose six points to 1,481.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,481 today from 1,475 on March 14, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1492    13.544	  1491    13.538</p>
<p>   1a   1474 11163.000	  1468 11119.000</p>
<p>   2    1798    25.688	  1794    25.625</p>
<p>   2a   1826 14975.000	  1820 14925.000</p>
<p>   3    1694    15.625	  1678    15.481</p>
<p>   3a   1558 12294.000	  1552 12250.000</p>
<p>   6    1237    12.763	  1236    12.750</p>
<p>   7    1158     5.638	  1157     5.631</p>
<p>   8     931    10.238	   930    10.225</p>
<p>   9     988  8638.000	   975  8525.000</p>
<p>  10    1097     5.544	  1096     5.538</p>
